e foliage of my trees, and but a few stray gleams steal into the inner sanctuary, I throw myself down among the tall grass by the trickling stream; and, as I lie close to the earth, a thousand unknown plants are noticed by me.\";s:10:\"text-align\";s:4:\"left\";s:14:\"padding-bottom\";s:4:\"30px\";}}}}}'),
